ols_tail_primitives_capsule_validation_receipt.json","receipts/acceptance/first_wave/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule_fixture_acceptance.json"],"receipt_time_basis":"historical_saved_artifact"},"formal_subclaim_ids":["subclaim::evidence_diff"],"primary_guide_id":"paper_module.batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule","primary_guide_ref":"paper_modules/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule.md","registered_runner_ref":"src/microcosm_core/organs/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule.py","replay_id":"replay::batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule","requirements_review":{"status":"unrecorded"},"summary":"Four copied tools run small diff, patch, identity and parsing examples.","title":"Exercise four copied tooling primitives"},"claim_ceiling":"verified non-secret macro body import only, not source authority, private-root equivalence, release, or publication","claim_ceiling_restated":"Runs four copied tools on small set-difference, document-patch, identity-hash and parser examples, and rejects malformed input and a ledger ID without an identity. The patch helper covers a subset of JSON Patch operations.","claim_id":"claim::batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule","evidence_class":"verified_macro_body_import","evidence_strength_rank":5,"organ_id":"batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"copied_non_secret_macro_body","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule run --input fixtures/first_wave/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule/input --out receipts/first_wave/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule_fixture_acceptance.json"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"e74e2d1858b5ae982235243bc5a0a2b186cf029107241b077fe6ea520527f441","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"verified_macro_body_import","family":"import_projection_and_drift","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"copied_non_secret_macro_body"},"component_id":"batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule","plain":"Small helper tools can fail on odd input, so they need trying on known cases. This check loads four copied helpers and gives them small example inputs. It divides the labels from two evidence lists into shared, missed and extra ones, edits a temporary document, tidies names, and notes a badly formed entry as a gap when reading sample files. The result is a status with findings, and the step that divides the labels is checked by a mathematical proof against written rules.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule.md","sha256":"122669417cd5cbbd77bab58c29542138b9da2bdf0c81ffcd68ad1995fe801b23","text":"# Exercise four copied tooling primitives\n\n> **In plain terms.** Small helper tools can fail on odd input, so they need trying on known cases. This check loads four copied helpers and gives them small example inputs. It divides the labels from two evidence lists into shared, missed and extra ones, edits a temporary document, tidies names, and notes a badly formed entry as a gap when reading sample files. The result is a status with findings, and the step that divides the labels is checked by a mathematical proof against written rules.\n\nThis fixture loads four copied modules and checks their output on small inputs. The observer diff divides evidence IDs into overlap, missed and extra sets and compares prediction rows; malformed rows without the required key are skipped. A patch helper applies `set`, `merge` and `append` to a temporary document. An identity helper normalizes lane names and derives IDs. A parser records coverage for synthetic miner, spine and prediction artifacts.\n\nThe negative cases check, among other things, that traversing a scalar during a patch raises an error, a stock record without its identity is refused, and a malformed tuple appears as a parser coverage gap.\n\n## Run the example\n\nPython 3.11 or newer and the project test dependencies (install with `python3 -m pip install -e \".[test]\"`) are required. Run from the repository root:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule run \\\n  --input fixtures/first_wave/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule/input \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule \\\n  --acceptance-out .microcosm/component-guides/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule/acceptance.json\n```\n\nThe command writes its result and acceptance files under `.microcosm/component-guides/`; inspect the status and findings in those files.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe evidence-ID exercise calls a [Dafny-verified partition core](../formal/components/evidence_diff/README.md). For the supplied finite ID sequences, it identifies IDs present in either or both inputs and the last occurrence in each. Python normalizes IDs, sorts and projects rows; prediction comparison and the other three primitives are outside this proof.\n\nThe direct fixture calls this core. Separately, `make component-replays` applies the [shared admission check](../formal/replay/README.md) to the component replay’s captured observations.\n\n## Limits\n\nRuns four copied tools on small set-difference, document-patch, identity-hash and parser examples, and rejects malformed input and a ledger ID without an identity. The patch helper covers a subset of JSON Patch operations.\n\n## Sources\n\n[src/microcosm_core/organs/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule.py](../src/microcosm_core/organs/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule.py) contains the implementation. See the [input fixtures](../fixtures/first_wave/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule/input/), [tests](../tests/test_batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule.py), [historical sample acceptance result](../receipts/acceptance/first_wave/batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule_fixture_acceptance.json), and the [component JSON record](../core/paper_module_capsules.json). For comparison, see [RFC 6902](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6902).\n"},"proofs":[{"claim_ids":["claim::batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule"],"component_ids":["batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule"],"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"guide":{"availability":"available","plain":null,"plain_availability":"unrecorded","ref":"formal/components/evidence_diff/README.md","sha256":"b1778c427e3e1553d2fca24c20dde3564bc435c367e95c40a2ac8031bfa32f35","text":"# Evidence ID partition\n\n`EvidenceDiff.dfy` computes a category and the final index for every normalized\nID. Its postcondition states that the four categories are exactly absent,\nlab-only, oracle-only and shared, and that each present index points to the last\noccurrence of that ID. Together these partition the union into extra, missed\nand shared IDs. The proof applies to any finite sequences of integer ranks\nwithin the supplied universe.\n\nThe Batch 8 tools-tail evidence exercise calls the generated kernel through\n`plectis.components.evidence_diff`. The trusted Python adapter turns JSON-safe\nscalar IDs into injective ranks using Python equality, chooses the original\nkey representatives, orders the result and projects original rows. JSON\nserialization, Python's equality and sorting behavior, the adapter, runtime,\ncompiler and host are outside the theorem. The copied observer's prediction\ncomparison is a separate, unproved computation; its source snapshot is kept.\n\nThe accompanying mutant changes the shared category into the missing category;\nDafny rejects the maintained invariant. `metadata.json` records the pinned\ncompiler, verified build, generated file hashes and mutant result. Rebuilding\nand comparing generated bytes is required before changing the source.\n"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot","modeled_contracts":[{"assumptions":"Trusted host supplies normalized observations; adapter, isolated worker, Dafny, compiler and runtime remain trusted.","contract_sha256":"f2dcb8de46ce738acec56c78920d442a433b1c56907ac021039f864a3db7b7f4","descriptor_origin":"metadata_contract","entry_theorem_refs":["formal/components/evidence_diff/EvidenceDiff.dfy#FindLast","formal/components/evidence_diff/EvidenceDiff.dfy#Compute"],"input_model":"Two finite sequences of integer ranks and a universe covering those ranks.","limits":"Host ID normalization, Python equality, sorting and projected rows are trusted; prediction comparison is separate.","requirements_review":{"status":"unrecorded"},"specification_refs":["formal/components/evidence_diff/EvidenceDiff.dfy#LastAt","formal/components/evidence_diff/EvidenceDiff.dfy#Classified"],"statement":"For each normalized ID, the core assigns absent, lab-only, oracle-only or shared and returns the last occurrence index.","subclaim_id":"subclaim::evidence_diff"}],"proof":{"adapter_ref":"src/plectis/components/evidence_diff/_adapter.py","claim_ids":["claim::batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule"],"component_ids":["batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule"],"current_binding":{"assessment_time_basis":"index_generation_only","checker_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_kernels.py#check_binding","generated_python":{"EvidenceDiff.py":"403095fd8ad89faddc7a044c5e9901d067d3badba6533bda3529c5457e8f1cb5","System_/__init__.py":"96b6e33c036bc3aeab6d1810c7aef085184d09c407bdec032ea89d7a98843edf","__main__.py":"694c23985cf61a2bbd5d9f93a6be83a5e3dba47a28169b63f1289b0787be9e18","_dafny/__init__.py":"18d39decdedad0e188456e15d17f1dcd5113c4abc258ad6cb718e39534555e7a","module_.py":"ad19df4df3b3c8fc28c50ed0b400a4c2a1793ccd91130003ddbae28cf8a0c4d4"},"source_sha256":"d752cd10b557ee247c249990a2dac160971ac972f5cb6579a34cec6ef920fa48","status":"current_hash_binding_pass"},"entry_theorem_refs":["formal/components/evidence_diff/EvidenceDiff.dfy#FindLast","formal/components/evidence_diff/EvidenceDiff.dfy#Compute"],"excerpts":[{"kind":"predicate","line_end":11,"line_start":7,"name":"LastAt","ref":"formal/components/evidence_diff/EvidenceDiff.dfy#LastAt","source_sha256":"d752cd10b557ee247c249990a2dac160971ac972f5cb6579a34cec6ef920fa48","text":"  predicate LastAt(s: seq<int>, key: int, index: int) {\n    if index == -1 then key !in s\n    else (0 <= index < |s| && s[index] == key &&\n      (forall j: int :: index < j < |s| ==> s[j] != key))\n  }\n","text_sha256":"3b72007525377cf066daee9e3ed8e00b76b393e9a76ab307ba2552e347574206"},{"kind":"predicate","line_end":21,"line_start":14,"name":"Classified","ref":"formal/components/evidence_diff/EvidenceDiff.dfy#Classified","source_sha256":"d752cd10b557ee247c249990a2dac160971ac972f5cb6579a34cec6ef920fa48","text":"  predicate Classified(s: seq<int>, t: seq<int>, key: int, c: Cell) {\n    LastAt(s, key, c.labLast) && LastAt(t, key, c.oracleLast) &&\n    (c.category == 0 <==> key !in s && key !in t) &&\n    (c.category == 1 <==> key in s && key !in t) &&\n    (c.category == 2 <==> key !in s && key in t) &&\n    (c.category == 3 <==> key in s && key in t) &&\n    0 <= c.category <= 3\n  }\n","text_sha256":"60ad5437036ab4eb905666399b2849ed6090342b20721dae06d7b7014176a84d"},{"kind":"method","line_end":39,"line_start":23,"name":"FindLast","ref":"formal/components/evidence_diff/EvidenceDiff.dfy#FindLast","source_sha256":"d752cd10b557ee247c249990a2dac160971ac972f5cb6579a34cec6ef920fa48","text":"  method FindLast(s: seq<int>, key: int) returns (index: int)\n    ensures LastAt(s, key, index)\n  {\n    var i := |s|;\n    while i > 0\n      invariant 0 <= i <= |s|\n      invariant forall j: int :: i <= j < |s| ==> s[j] != key\n      decreases i\n    {\n      i := i - 1;\n      if s[i] == key {\n        index := i;\n        return;\n      }\n    }\n    index := -1;\n  }\n","text_sha256":"01daf115dc02f38500653e1c4d988f97071077a3ffcadc29ae374c94b1f9c1c6"},{"kind":"method","line_end":61,"line_start":41,"name":"Compute","ref":"formal/components/evidence_diff/EvidenceDiff.dfy#Compute","source_sha256":"d752cd10b557ee247c249990a2dac160971ac972f5cb6579a34cec6ef920fa48","text":"  method Compute(lab: seq<int>, oracle: seq<int>, size: nat) returns (cells: seq<Cell>)\n    requires forall i: int :: 0 <= i < |lab| ==> 0 <= lab[i] < size\n    requires forall i: int :: 0 <= i < |oracle| ==> 0 <= oracle[i] < size\n    ensures |cells| == size\n    ensures forall key: int :: 0 <= key < size ==> Classified(lab, oracle, key, cells[key])\n  {\n    cells := [];\n    var key: nat := 0;\n    while key < size\n      invariant key <= size\n      invariant |cells| == key\n      invariant forall k: int :: 0 <= k < key ==> Classified(lab, oracle, k, cells[k])\n      decreases size - key\n    {\n      var l := FindLast(lab, key);\n      var o := FindLast(oracle, key);\n      var kind := if l < 0 then (if o < 0 then 0 else 2) else (if o < 0 then 1 else 3);\n      cells := cells + [Cell(l, o, kind)];\n      key := key + 1;\n    }\n  }\n","text_sha256":"9e99cf09df4637ef0916bd7c54b7ac149c9df0f8e09a80fc176ef5820b0e1c7c"}],"fresh_prover_result":{"status":"not_run_by_index"},"generated_refs":["src/plectis/components/evidence_diff/_generated/EvidenceDiff.py","src/plectis/components/evidence_diff/_generated/System_/__init__.py","src/plectis/components/evidence_diff/_generated/__main__.py","src/plectis/components/evidence_diff/_generated/_dafny/__init__.py","src/plectis/components/evidence_diff/_generated/module_.py"],"guide":{"availability":"available","plain":null,"plain_availability":"unrecorded","ref":"formal/components/evidence_diff/README.md","sha256":"b1778c427e3e1553d2fca24c20dde3564bc435c367e95c40a2ac8031bfa32f35","text":"# Evidence ID partition\n\n`EvidenceDiff.dfy` computes a category and the final index for every normalized\nID. Its postcondition states that the four categories are exactly absent,\nlab-only, oracle-only and shared, and that each present index points to the last\noccurrence of that ID. Together these partition the union into extra, missed\nand shared IDs. The proof applies to any finite sequences of integer ranks\nwithin the supplied universe.\n\nThe Batch 8 tools-tail evidence exercise calls the generated kernel through\n`plectis.components.evidence_diff`. The trusted Python adapter turns JSON-safe\nscalar IDs into injective ranks using Python equality, chooses the original\nkey representatives, orders the result and projects original rows. JSON\nserialization, Python's equality and sorting behavior, the adapter, runtime,\ncompiler and host are outside the theorem. The copied observer's prediction\ncomparison is a separate, unproved computation; its source snapshot is kept.\n\nThe accompanying mutant changes the shared category into the missing category;\nDafny rejects the maintained invariant. `metadata.json` records the pinned\ncompiler, verified build, generated file hashes and mutant result. Rebuilding\nand comparing generated bytes is required before changing the source.\n"},"language":"dafny","metadata_ref":"formal/components/evidence_diff/metadata.json","module":"EvidenceDiff","negative_controls":[{"changed_lines":[{"line":57,"mutated":"      var kind := if l < 0 then (if o < 0 then 0 else 2) else (if o < 0 then 1 else 2);","original":"      var kind := if l < 0 then (if o < 0 then 0 else 2) else (if o < 0 then 1 else 3);"}],"changed_lines_sha256":"c37eb1853042a3cb0b6312481fb54081956c9e9c1f6430125b143fa1213773a8","description":"Replaces 'else (if o < 0 then 1 else 3)' with 'else (if o < 0 then 1 else 2)'.","description_basis":"retained_mutation_recipe","fresh_result":{"status":"not_run_by_index"},"retained_result":{"basis":"recorded_metadata","errors":1,"verified_tasks":3},"source_re